KZ3 patch 1000-spu (SPU pass 81, the v0.15.0 bump): revert upstream PR #287 (NoahBPeterson, merge 41c19c8:
hardware-exact SPU float semantics, NEON paths, interpreter op fixes, the RPCS3-oracle differential tests and
the SPU op benchmark). Our SPU helper stack (1035, 1038-1041, 1071, 1079, 1082, 1088, 1089, 1095, 1097, 1102,
1105, 1106, 1108) was built and measured on the v0.13.0 spu_helpers.h; #287 rewrote 1,422 lines of it with
different float rules (extended range, denormals) and helper shapes. Keeping ours is the measured state; taking
#287 needs its own round (job-diff on all 75 modules + K2/K4 A/B). Interpreter ops #287 had are kept in 1003.
ASSUMPTION: nothing else in v0.15.0 depends on #287's helpers (the revert applied cleanly; its tests go with it).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): still a full revert of spu_helpers.h, now also of #445/#479/#500/#512 (SSE4.1/AVX2 forms), set to the old 1000 result; `spu_interp.c` keeps upstream #417 (interrupt E/D bits on taken indirect branches); deletes the helper-lineage tests test_spu_float_est/exact/rz_mode, test_spu_int_x86.c, tools/test_spu_float_rz_mode.py and the CMake test_spu_float_exact entry. Taking #512/#500 = its own round (job diff + A/B).

